※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4208 LANG_TYPE_OPERAND_NOT_BOOLEAN

※ The logical operators join truth values.  A number is not one: there is no
※ rule here that anything other than zero counts as true, which is where a
※ good deal of C's trouble comes from.  Where the question is whether a number
※ is zero, '≠' asks it.
let count: u8 = 3u8
let ready: bool = true

@[startup]
fn main() → bool:
    count ∧ ready
